# The field axioms as properties: a field is a set with addition and multiplication where addition is an abelian group,
# nonzero multiplication is an abelian group, and multiplication distributes over addition. The scalar-compatibility
# properties (that scaling a vector by a product of field elements equals scaling twice, and that the field identity
# scales trivially) are the laws tying a vector space to its field of scalars. These are universal equations the field
# and vector-space forms satisfy; the structures themselves are in the structure folder.
